00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:06.060
so they say like, "Hey you."

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.226
- Yeah, that's very disrespectful.

00:01:08.226 --> 00:01:09.059
- Yeah.

00:01:09.059 --> 00:01:10.930
- I've had people straight
up yell at me from

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:12.508
across the restaurant and I'm just like,

00:01:12.508 --> 00:01:15.560
"I didn't hear you, I'm
gonna go do something else."

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.227
- When somebody orders something,

00:01:17.227 --> 00:01:18.130
"How do you want it cooked?"

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:18.963
You know.

00:01:18.963 --> 00:01:20.580
"Well done, rare, da da da da da."

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.000
So they'll ask for it well done.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.057
It comes out well done,
it's too well done.

00:01:24.057 --> 00:01:25.025
"You asked for it that way."

00:01:25.025 --> 00:01:28.047
So I'll remake it a little
less well done this time.

00:01:28.047 --> 00:01:29.010
"It's not cooked enough."

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.690
You (bleep) kidding me?

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.940
- You come into a place,
you have allergies

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.607
to certain things, and
it's like, "Why come here?"

00:01:34.607 --> 00:01:36.990
People who've had gluten allergies,

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.730
flour allergies, bread allergies,

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.700
and you come into a pizza
restaurant, you know?

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.117
You can't have flour,
you can't have gluten,

00:01:42.117 --> 00:01:43.490
can't have cheese.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.040
I mean, suppose to give you ice cubes?

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.285
- It's like watching the insane ways

