the (bleep) ceiling,

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.357
I understand it's our job to
clean the restaurant and stuff,

00:02:26.357 --> 00:02:28.010
but at least pick up after your kids.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:30.340
Don't let them create mayhem
and then just walk away

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.420
and be like, "Ah, all right, later,"

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.340
and then not tip either.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.078
- I always give the customers
napkins when I see that stuff.

00:02:36.078 --> 00:02:37.680
I'm like, "Oh, here you guys go."

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:38.750
- Rude people, man.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:39.690
Very impatient.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.530
- The impatience thing
with me is a big one

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:43.000
when people try and slip you money

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.393
and expect to get a table
faster, or if they hit on you,

00:02:45.393 --> 00:02:46.737
and it's like, "Why?

00:02:46.737 --> 00:02:48.500
"Why do you think that I would like that?"

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.665
But one guy actually did
slip me a twenty once,

00:02:50.665 --> 00:02:53.420
